From: OpenWrt WR11000 port
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: compare user country against what firmware was sent

ath12k_reg_notifier() skips a user regulatory hint when its alpha2 equals
hw->wiphy->regd. That regd only tracks the last regulatory event ath12k
accepted, not the country the firmware is actually running.

Seen on IPQ5332 + QCN9274 (Cudy WR11000): a fresh OpenWrt config sets
country "00" on the 6 GHz radio. The firmware applies it and replies with
status PASS and zero rules; ath12k rejects that event ("No reg rules
available"), so wiphy->regd keeps the boot-time "US". When the user then
sets "US", the notifier sees no change and never sends it. The firmware
stays on "00" and refuses every DFS channel ("vdev start resp error
status 4 (invalid regdomain)").

Forwarding every hint instead fixes that, but OpenWrt re-sets the country
on every wifi reload; each resend makes the firmware re-apply it, the
channel list is rebuilt, DFS channel state is reset and a 5 GHz AP on a
DFS channel is stopped.

So skip only when the country matches what was last sent to every radio
(ar->alpha2, which the current-country and 11d paths already maintain).
Record it in the init-country path too.

Known gap: after a firmware crash the init-country path does not resend
ar->alpha2 (only current_cc_support devices do), so a non-default country
is not restored until it changes.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/reg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/reg.c
@@ -92,9 +92,27 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* hw->wiphy->regd only reflects the last regulatory event ath12k
+	 * accepted. A request the firmware applies but answers with no
+	 * rules (alpha2 "00") is dropped, so wiphy->regd keeps the boot
+	 * country while the firmware runs "00". Compare against what was
+	 * last sent to every radio instead, so the user's country still
+	 * goes out once, and repeated identical requests (every wifi
+	 * reload) do not make the firmware re-apply it and reset the DFS
+	 * state of a running AP.
+	 */
 	if (!ath12k_regdom_changes(hw, request->alpha2)) {
-		ath12k_dbg(ar->ab, ATH12K_DBG_REG, "Country is already set\n");
-		return;
+		bool sent = true;
+
+		for_each_ar(ah, ar, i)
+			if (memcmp(ar->alpha2, request->alpha2, 2))
+				sent = false;
+
+		ar = ath12k_ah_to_ar(ah, 0);
+		if (sent) {
+			ath12k_dbg(ar->ab, ATH12K_DBG_REG, "Country is already set\n");
+			return;
+		}
 	}
 
 	/* Allow fresh updates to wiphy regd */
@@ -115,6 +133,7 @@
 			arg.flags = ALPHA_IS_SET;
 			memcpy(&arg.cc_info.alpha2, request->alpha2, 2);
 			arg.cc_info.alpha2[2] = 0;
+			memcpy(&ar->alpha2, request->alpha2, 2);
 
 			ret = ath12k_wmi_send_init_country_cmd(ar, &arg);
 			if (ret)
